Zero distinct-syntax source migration

All six active system/tool sources now use the same distinct grammar:
bios.zero, kernel.zero, loader.zero, loader32.zero, image.zero and iso.zero.
Examples, active valid/invalid/boundary fixtures and real-mode.zero were also
migrated. Source comments, operation order, constants and algorithms were
preserved. There is no packaged foreign-language source converter or runtime.

Syntax conventions
An expression followed by => @name. creates a variable. An expression followed
by -> @name. updates an existing variable. References always begin with @.
? condition [ ... ] ~ [ ... ] is a choice; the alternative is optional.
?? condition [ ... ] repeats its block while the condition is nonzero.
:operation[argument|argument] yields a value; !operation[arguments]. performs
an effect. Zero-argument architectural effects include !halt. and !disable.
Parentheses remain available for arithmetic grouping. See SYNTAX.ztext for
the complete grammar and the retained u64/u32 target contracts.

Verification performed during migration
PASS: all six active sources compile with the new grammar for their target.
PASS: five native language regression programs produce the original exact
      expected output and exit successfully.
PASS: all 24 invalid fixtures reject with status 1 and zero stdout. Each was
      rewritten to exercise its original semantic or grammar failure.
PASS: source byte limits (65536 accepted, 65537 rejected), 64 variables,
      31-character names, 64 block levels, expression-depth and output limits.
PASS: raw target fixture compiles with its memory/port operations.
PASS: migrated real-mode regression compiles byte-for-byte identically to
      the previously validated real-mode regression binary.
PASS: migrated kernel, EFI64 loader, FAT builder and ISO builder compile
      byte-for-byte identically to their pre-migration sources compiled by
      the previous compiler. This checks grammar migration independently
      of changes already made to those source algorithms before migration.

The new IA32 loader/backend and BIOS protected-mode branch are integration
work in the same release. Their runtime results belong in verification.ztext;
successful source migration alone is not claimed as a VM boot test.

Active packaged tests are examples/, review-tests/valid/, invalid/, boundary/,
TESTS.ztext and real-mode.zero. Older loader-faults-0.2.2 and uefi-review working
directories are historical audit artifacts and are not current test sources.
